Version 0.02 (2026-11-01; the corwin branch; unreleased)

- topology forge (formerly TopoForge) 1.11: a pad on the overview map (a
  drawn slider for its mode, an arm for its scale, a grip to move it) and
  Reset layout, for a page that asks.  See topoforge/NEWS.

- topology forge (formerly TopoForge) 1.10: the overview map's three modes
  for a page's preview (a card, the card with the matches lit in the
  drawing, or rings), the map's own scale, and the wheel over the map.
  See topoforge/NEWS.

- topology paint, made for Bryant Frankford (paint/): a drawing and
  painting program in C for Windows, Linux and macOS.  Pen pressure and
  tilt through SDL3 (Windows Ink, XInput2 and Wayland, macOS), a pressure
  curve with a live meter, 12 brushes plus brush files, up to 256 layers
  with 13 blend modes, undo, autosave, and OpenRaster and Photoshop files
  with their layers, PNG, JPEG, TIFF, BMP, TGA, QOI and PPM.  Mods add
  filters, formats and brush tips.  paint/build.bat or paint/build.sh
  builds, installs and updates it; sh bin/test.sh now checks its core
  (77 checks, two planted faults).  See paint/README.md.

- topology forge (formerly TopoForge) 1.9, by Bryant Frankford, with our
  changes: calls and switches a page that embeds it asked for (the view,
  where the selection is, keys and right clicks for the page, setting a
  shape's fields, a message when pages change), all off when the app is
  opened on its own.  Also new: the overview map moved and resized by
  handles that appear as you reach for it, a preview in it for a page that
  asks, and, everywhere, page tabs that do not fit shown with < and > and a
  list of them all, in place of a scrolling strip.  See topoforge/NEWS.

- The drawing app is topology forge (formerly TopoForge), 1.8, made by
  Bryant Frankford; its work now goes on here.  README.org says how it is
  named.  New in 1.8: switches a page that embeds it may turn on (no frame,
  floating Properties and Shapes, page tabs in the overview map, a
  selection hook and a ready event, same origin only), all off when the app
  is opened on its own, which looks as 1.7 did.  See topoforge/NEWS.

- TopoForge's own test kits, story spec, project files and recipe now live
  in topoforge/, and sh bin/test.sh runs them against the app in
  www/topoforge/ (unchanged).

- The app gives the drawing the whole width.  Its settings are one closed
  line above it; Draw and Go appear only once a graph server is chosen;
  Copy as a prompt now carries the drawing's own story, as TopoForge writes it.

- The pages use the egad design system's colours by default, light and dark;
  the app can switch back to the first palette or fix light or dark.
- Both pages were audited against WCAG 2.1 AA: a main landmark and heading
  in the app, skip links that land on something that takes focus, labelled
  fields, keyboard-reachable code blocks, input edges at 3:1, less motion.
  tests/a11y-check.mjs keeps them that way.
- examples/inputloop/ draws inputloop's own hosts, projects, tools, paths
  and people, with the four private projects hidden by the show-private rule.

Version 0.01 (2026-10-31; the corwin branch; built and tested, not yet deployed)

- Draw what you have: topology reads the git repositories you list, the
  TOPOLOGY.md (and .topology.md) files in them, and draws the result with
  TopoForge.
- Zero Sharing: the browser app works with no server; settings and
  drawings stay in the browser; export them at any time.  When saved
  settings need an upgrade, each change is shown, Accept all jumps to a
  summary grouped by where, what, how and who, and nothing changes before
  ACCEPT.  Export before, and after by ticking a box.
- Private parts of TOPOLOGY.md: show, hide or auto per container;
  always, never or auto everywhere; auto asks the component's own file;
  when its two files disagree, the part stays hidden and the app says so.
- Three Debian packages: topology-www (files only), topology-perl (perl
  5.44.0 with sixteen CPAN modules), topology (command, API, settings).
- Every feature can be switched off; "ceiling = spa" leaves only the app's
  files.  Go (letting tools make a change) is off by default.
